[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: injected store (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mlogin(username, password, identity). Literal third parameter, testable without a DOM, subscriptions can be added [39m
     [38;5;246mlater without changing callers.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: singleton + return value
     [38;5;246mlogin imports the store and returns the userId. Least code, most conventional, but adds no parameter and is harder
[39m     [38;5;246mto test.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: event-driven store
     [38;5;246mStore notifies subscribers, with cross-tab sync. Best for many future consumers; most machinery for the one [39m
     [38;5;246mconsumer that exists today.[39m
